<h1>Maria Pappas</h1>
<p>Cook County Treasurer. Candidate for mayor of Chicago, on the ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<p>County Treasurer since 1998 and a county commissioner before that; 77, born in a Greek family restaurant in West Virginia, with four degrees including a PhD and a law degree. Filed just under 40,000 signatures on the last day and says her campaign starts in earnest after the November treasurer race.</p>
<h2>What sets them apart</h2>
<p>Not published: No campaign site and no positions on taxes, pensions, housing, or schools as of November. Pappas said the campaign would start after the November 3 county election.</p>
<p>The pitch: County treasurer since 1998, promising to dig through the city budget line by line.</p>
<p>Only Pappas: Ties every neighborhood&#39;s property tax bill to the health of the Loop, citing her office&#39;s tax studies.</p>
<h2>In their words</h2>
<ul>
<li>Argues that what happens to the Loop decides what happens to every neighborhood&#39;s property taxes. <q>When the Loop gets a cold, the rest of the city gets pneumonia,</q> (<a href="https://chicago.suntimes.com/elections/2025/11/18/cook-county-treasurer-maria-pappas-mayoral-campaign-chicago-brandon-johnson" rel="nofollow noopener">Treasurer&#39;s office release, Nov. 18, 2025 (Sun-Times)</a>)</li>
<li>Would dig through the city budget line by line. <q>Get down to all the dirt, dig it up, and go &#39;Oh, this is the mess we&#39;ve created? How am I gonna fix it?&#39;</q> (<a href="https://www.audacy.com/wbbm780/news/local/pappas-im-going-to-get-in-the-mayors-race" rel="nofollow noopener">WBBM Newsradio, Nov. 18, 2025</a>)</li>
<li>Says the city can be fixed but needs a plan, and promises to be a mayor out in the streets. <q>The city&#39;s salvageable. It can be fixed. But you need a plan.</q> (<a href="https://www.audacy.com/wbbm780/news/local/pappas-im-going-to-get-in-the-mayors-race" rel="nofollow noopener">WBBM Newsradio, Nov. 18, 2025</a>)</li>
<li>Says what the city needs is a grandmother in charge. <q>The city NEEDS a grey-haired grandmother!</q> (<a href="https://www.audacy.com/wbbm780/news/local/pappas-im-going-to-get-in-the-mayors-race" rel="nofollow noopener">WBBM Newsradio, Nov. 18, 2025</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Campaign money</h2>
<ul>
<li>Committee: Committee to Elect Maria Pappas</li>
<li>Raised: $0</li>
<li>Spent: $52K</li>
<li>Cash on hand: $226K</li>
<li>Raised July 1 to Sept. 30, 2026; spent Jan. 1 to Sept. 30, 2026. Her committee was running for county treasurer, not mayor, through September. <a href="https://illinoissunshine.org/committees/6051/" rel="nofollow noopener">Source</a></li>
</ul>
<p>Money figures are each committee&#39;s quarterly reports to the Illinois State Board of Elections: spent is total expenditures from January 1 to September 30, 2026 (or since the committee formed), cash is funds available on September 30.</p>
<h2>Support</h2>
<p>3.3% of likely voters in the ChicagoSpeaks poll, Sept. 2026 (Mansueto Institute / NORC). 63 points of support per $1 million spent.</p>
<h2>On money</h2>
<p>Would go through the city budget with what she calls a fork and a shovel, and ties the whole city&#39;s property tax burden to the health of the Loop.</p>
<ul>
<li><q>Get down to all the dirt, dig it up, and go &#39;Oh, this is the mess we&#39;ve created? How am I gonna fix it?&#39;</q> (<a href="https://www.audacy.com/wbbm780/news/local/pappas-im-going-to-get-in-the-mayors-race" rel="nofollow noopener">WBBM Newsradio, Nov. 18, 2025</a>)</li>
<li><q>When the Loop gets a cold, the rest of the city gets pneumonia,</q> (<a href="https://chicago.suntimes.com/elections/2025/11/18/cook-county-treasurer-maria-pappas-mayoral-campaign-chicago-brandon-johnson" rel="nofollow noopener">Treasurer&#39;s office release, Nov. 18, 2025 (Sun-Times)</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Pizza</h2>
<p>No position on record.</p>
<h2>Also on the record</h2>
<ul>
<li>A prize-winning baton twirler who twirled a plunger on camera when no baton was handy. (<a href="https://www.axios.com/local/chicago/2025/05/09/cook-county-treasurer-maria-pappas-announcement" rel="nofollow noopener">axios.com</a>)</li>
<li>Filed her petitions wearing a shirt that read No biceps, just brains. (<a href="https://chicago.suntimes.com/elections/2026/10/26/chicago-mayoral-race-last-day-of-filing-mendoza-pappas-2027-election" rel="nofollow noopener">chicago.suntimes.com</a>)</li>
</ul>
